{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Then it passes on</b> like wind through every place, and further it commits a great offense, for it says, 'this is its god's strength' — not HaShem's. And it used אלהו in the singular as a term of contempt. Or it is the linguistic usage, to say: every man, as he pleases, אלהו or אלהיו — for this is customary."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:56.841560598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}